# Git Workflow

- Conventional Commits (`feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `test`, `chore`, `ci`, `refactor`).
- Do not commit secrets, `.env`, customer PDFs, or passwords.
- Do not mix unrelated concerns in one commit.
- Prefer `feature/*`, `fix/*`, `docs/*` branches; keep `main` release-ready.
- Only commit when the user requests it (unless executing an explicitly approved phase checklist that includes commits).
- Never force-push `main` or skip hooks unless the user explicitly requires it.
